PulseBridge ${environment}: what to do next (full runbook with checks: infra/envs/README.md)
Run from infra/envs/${environment}. "Deployer" = the bootstrap deployer account (or a person
with the same roles); "owner" = the project owner. Step numbers are the README's.

%{ if !ingest_enabled ~}
You are at ingest_enabled = false: steps 8 to 10 come before the second apply.

 5. (If not done yet) secret versions, without a trailing newline:
    ${secret_prefix}-db-root-password, ${secret_prefix}-openemr-db-password,
    ${secret_prefix}-openemr-admin-password, ${secret_prefix}-reviewer-password.
    Never write ${secret_prefix}-openemr-client-private-key: the VM does.
 8. First boot of ${vm_name} (${vm_zone}): about 15 minutes. Work through the edge-vm
    checklist, then the openemr checklist (README, step 8). Startup log:
      gcloud compute instances get-serial-port-output ${vm_name} --zone ${vm_zone} --project ${project_id}
    Done when it shows "hook openemr-oauth-client: ok" and "edge VM startup: done, all steps ok".
%{ if use_synthetic_data ~}
 9. First seeding (synthetic data; deployer). Wait for it to finish:
      gcloud run jobs execute ${seed_job_name} --region ${region} --project ${project_id} \
        --args=--days,30 --task-timeout=1800s --wait
    NEVER run the Google Health connect script in this deployment (SYN- patient).
%{ else ~}
 9. Connect Google Health (real data; you, with your own credentials):
      terraform output -raw setup_env > ~/pulsebridge-${environment}.env   # outside the repo
      # add your name, gender and birth date to that file (connect script README, "Run it")
      source ~/pulsebridge-${environment}.env && scripts/connect-google-health/connect.sh
%{ endif ~}
10. Second apply: set ingest_enabled = true in terraform.tfvars, then terraform apply.
    It creates the Scheduler job and switches the HL7v2 subscription to push.
%{ else ~}
ingest_enabled = true: the Scheduler job and the push subscription are on.
%{ endif ~}
11. Deploy the page (deployer, after every apply):
      terraform output -raw firebase_json > ../../../web/firebase.json
      (cd ../../../web && npm ci && npm run build && \
       npx --yes firebase-tools@<pinned version> deploy --only hosting --project ${project_id} --non-interactive)
12. First-deploy checks of the front door, hop measurement first (README, step 12).
    Page: ${dashboard_url}   Direct proxy URL (measurement only): terraform output -raw fhir_proxy_url
13. Ingestion checks: first and second run, alerts (README, step 13).
14. End-to-end check (T29, tests/e2e/).

Record each result in the master checklist (README, "Master checklist").
